From 9ed95b028d976187f6cdde2ded7f27b21a0c9f9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Snyder <73651542+mssnyder@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 14:59:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat: implement puppet warp skeletal animation

Adds skeletal animation support for puppet warp images (MDLV0013/0021/0023):

- Parse MDLS bone hierarchies (versions 0001/0003) and MDLA keyframe
  animations (versions 0001/0006), including multi-animation files and
  the zero footer between animations
- CPU-skin puppet meshes per frame (4 bone influences per vertex) and
  select animations via the object's animationlayers (id, rate, visible)
- Flatten z after skinning: 3D bone rotations otherwise push vertices
  outside the FBO ortho clip range, cutting the mesh
- Negate x/z rotation angles: animations are authored in WE's y-down
  space while the mesh lives in y-up coordinates
- Implement autosize for puppets: measure the skinned mesh across all
  animation frames and grow the canvas so animated limbs never clip
- Treat model cropoffset as editor-only metadata (applying it as a
  quad or mesh offset misplaces multi-piece characters)
- Move resolveTransform/localTransform from CImage to CObject and use
  them in CText so text objects honor parent chains; anchor text quads
  at the top edge and fix the scene y mapping

Also includes earlier parser fixes for wallpapers that failed to load:
optional orthogonalprojection, flexible text padding formats, optional
text property values, and the cropoffset model field.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
